\ge \\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328531/field-1" "q-328531/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca43484-4a4f-57b7-a4c2-23d1db997afd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328531"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651/selection/9428b228a91978b57bbd43ebbcd93d67ef456f0b613ee71b26de106a78b2c2ed" :answer/id #uuid "900974c1-5aec-5d04-bf41-25c4b9a237f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" :answer/id #uuid "2e36259d-0ad2-54db-bb24-8009564c8044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651/selection/ad2f8e8c0ea9ee9695c15030eb3e1b745087a9b672ab8f7c8a2af2fa6ec5202c" :answer/id #uuid "8c1516af-ec1e-514a-a033-49dc4ceff642" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651/selection/6ed514d1edca76ba0214d1b422746145281874a0da49fd7aaac25b01808d629b" :answer/id #uuid "0cb38c30-f6dd-524f-904c-cc60ea40aa8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge \\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651/selection/50f38497ce427b0c1c9d05990e08eed2c05d9dac45ab0e2d2e1aed9d6a2089f8" :answer/id #uuid "9697af63-e10d-5d4a-9017-feecd9bf56ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le \\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "78d426cb-1dd7-5e7e-9b01-c4e0b07ed868" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89651/selection/50f38497ce427b0c1c9d05990e08eed2c05d9dac45ab0e2d2e1aed9d6a2089f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-89651/selection/9428b228a91978b57bbd43ebbcd93d67ef456f0b613ee71b26de106a78b2c2ed" "q-89651/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" "q-89651/selection/ad2f8e8c0ea9ee9695c15030eb3e1b745087a9b672ab8f7c8a2af2fa6ec5202c" "q-89651/selection/6ed514d1edca76ba0214d1b422746145281874a0da49fd7aaac25b01808d629b" "q-89651/selection/50f38497ce427b0c1c9d05990e08eed2c05d9dac45ab0e2d2e1aed9d6a2089f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89651" :question/id #uuid "62752f35-a978-5f90-a8a9-d9ceb9f7ef79" :question/math-academy-id "q-89651" :question/problem "Solve the inequality\n\n$$\n\\frac{2{x}^{4}+3x}{{x}^{4}+2}\\le 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the denominator ${x}^{4}+2$ is positive for all values of $x.$ So, we can multiply both sides of the inequality by ${x}^{4}+2$ and solve the resulting inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{4}+3x}{{x}^{4}+2} & \\le 2 \\\\ ({x}^{4}+2)\\cdot \\frac{2{x}^{4}+3x}{{x}^{4}+2} & \\le ({x}^{4}+2)\\cdot 2 \\\\ 2{x}^{4}+3x & \\le 2{x}^{4}+4 \\\\ 3x & \\le 4 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89651/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca43484-4a4f-57b7-a4c2-23d1db997afd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328412/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "2a2d580d-166e-5bf8-86d4-f06ca378bdad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328412/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7d94646-4631-5ab3-8ef9-039fca06c15d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328412/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-328412/field-1/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328412/field-2/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa" :answer/id #uuid "fb136138-89cf-5bc6-b9d4-4d5614064553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328412/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d0ac08d-0cdf-5354-be1f-b7db0ef51474" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328412/field-2/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa" :answer-field/choices ["q-328412/field-2/f7e51073a8044d706f62a310ce4d8f162b2fb8c60dce078b4b3b822d9f8ed6fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328412" :question/id #uuid "b89b9610-96ff-53fd-8e92-9072d2639177" :question/math-academy-id "q-328412" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\frac{9-2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3}>\\frac{x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3}.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the denominator $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3$ is always positive. We know this because\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1\\,⇒\\,2\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\le 4.\n$$\n\nSo, we can multiply both sides of the inequality by $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3$ and solve the resulting inequality as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9-2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3} & >\\frac{x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3} \\\\ (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3)\\cdot \\frac{9-2x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3} & >(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3)\\cdot \\frac{x-1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3} \\\\ 9-2x & >x-1 \\\\ -3x & >-10 \\\\ x & <\\,\\frac{10}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328412/field-1" "q-328412/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bca43484-4a4f-57b7-a4c2-23d1db997afd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328530/field-1/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer/id #uuid "dd083002-5050-5163-a223-294d5147c3db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328530/field-1/e4e9dbe